1	/**
2	 * The refusal census: every refusal this repository can emit from the code the
3	 * migration pipeline is made of, with its exact string, the condition that
4	 * raises it, and whose decision it is.
5	 *
6	 * The census is derived, not written. Each entry is read out of the source by
7	 * parsing it — the message from the thrown expression, the condition from the
8	 * guard the throw sits under, the location from the node — so a refusal cannot
9	 * be added, reworded or deleted in source without the census moving with it.
10	 * A hand-maintained list would be wrong within a week and would be wrong
11	 * silently, which is the failure mode this document exists to prevent.
12	 *
13	 * Two scopes are deliberate.
14	 *
15	 * The pipeline's own refusals are the `refuse()` call sites in
16	 * `packages/cli/src/operator/**`; those carry their own code, stage and origin,
17	 * and the census reads them rather than inventing any. A plain `throw` left in
18	 * those files is recorded as a **defect**, not as a refusal — that distinction
19	 * is the whole reason the exit codes differ.
20	 *
21	 * The frozen subtrees are enumerated read-only. T001 enumerated the 21 throws
22	 * in the operator flows and said so explicitly; the adapters were never
23	 * counted. They are counted here. Nothing in this module writes into a frozen
24	 * path, and the census records the freeze composite it was read at so a later
25	 * reader can tell whether it is still current.
26	 */
